calNodeIds":["cnm_p169"],"coverage":"partial","flags":[],"questionId":"1992_AMC_8_Q02","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p165","cnm_p166"],"id":"compare-fraction-representations","label":"Express the choices in fourths","methodDirectNodeIds":{"compare-fraction-representations":["cnm_p167","cnm_p168","cnm_p169"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p167","cnm_p168","cnm_p169","cnm_p165","cnm_p166"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:de3c5f138eafbd29f92829e1"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B. February, with an excess of 66⅔%","reason":"In equal graph blocks, the monthly pairs are (7,9), (5,3), (9,6), (9,12) and (8,10). Their relative excesses are 2/7, 2/3, 1/2, 1/3 and 1/4. February is greatest.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p169"],"coverage":"partial","flags":[],"questionId":"1992_AMC_8_Q21","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p108","cnm_p197","cnm_p169"],"id":"compare_relative_excess","label":"Compare each difference with the smaller sale","methodDirectNodeIds":{"compare_relative_excess":["cnm_p130","cnm_p205"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p130","cnm_p205","cnm_p108","cnm_p197","cnm_p169"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:de3c5f138eafbd29f92829e1"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, Friday","reason":"If M_n is the millet just after the nth addition, M_1 = 1/4 and M_n = (3/4)M_(n-1)+1/4. Millet exceeds half the seeds exactly when M_n > 3/4. Thursday gives 175/256 < 3/4, while Friday gives 781/1024 > 3/4.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p169"],"coverage":"partial","flags":[],"questionId":"2009_AMC_10B_Q14","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p196","cnm_p178","cnm_p173","cnm_p169"],"id":"daily-millet-amount","label":"Track the millet after each refill","methodDirectNodeIds":{"daily-millet-amount":["cnm_h200"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h200","cnm_p196","cnm_p178","cnm_p173","cnm_p169"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p196","cnm_p178","cnm_p169"],"id":"reference-amount-shortfall","label":"Track the shortfall from a reference amount","methodDirectNodeIds":{"reference-amount-shortfall":["cnm_h200","cnm_015"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h200","cnm_015","cnm_p196","cnm_p178","cnm_p169"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:de3c5f138eafbd29f92829e1"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 50/99","reason":"For even x, the smallest integer numerator above x/2 gives slope at least 51/100. For odd x ≤ 99, it gives slope at least 1/2 + 1/198 = 50/99. This slope passes through (99,52), so the open interval can end at 50/99 but cannot extend beyond it.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p169"],"coverage":"partial","flags":[],"questionId":"2011_AMC_10B_Q24","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_082","cnm_p169","cnm_096"],"id":"solution:denominator-parity-bound:d349294b24f3","label":"Find the first slope that reaches a lattice point","methodDirectNodeIds":{"denominator-parity-bound":["math:extremal-principle","cnm_p156"]},"nodeIds":["math:extremal-principle","cnm_p156","cnm_082","cnm_p169","cnm_096"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"alignmentIds":["alignment:de3c5f138eafbd29f92829e1"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, 50/99","reason":"Write a forbidden slope as p/q=(y-2)/x, where 1≤q≤100. For odd q, its smallest value above 1/2 is 1/2+1/(2q), minimized at q=99. For even q it is at least 1/2+1/100, which is larger. Hence the first forbidden slope is 50/99, attained at (99,52). Since m<a is strict, a=50/99 is allowed.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p169"],"coverage":"partial","flags":[],"questionId":"2011_AMC_12B_Q19","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_082","cnm_p156","cnm_p169"],"id":"nearest-forbidden-slope","label":"Find the first slope that reaches a lattice point","methodDirectNodeIds